I’m thinking about how content scripts can access DOM properties but not page-defined JavaScript properties. They often require script injection for that. It also raises the question of whether Figma defines `window.figma` as an accessor that behaves differently based on the caller or origin. I wonder if `window.figma` acts as a proxy object from an extension function because of Content Security Policy (CSP). There's also the possibility that it has a null prototype."},{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Testing and editing build**

I need to work on the test build now. Let's edit it to ensure everything is functioning correctly. Additionally, I see that the content type "BridgeResponse" has been restored, which is good, but I plan to make some changes to it as well. There seems to be quite a bit to consider, but I’ll take my time to make sure it’s all correct. Everything needs to fall into place!"}]}

